  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed to target and provoke individuals who hold or are exposed to anti-Black racial stereotypes, particularly those who believe Black people are not 'American enough' to celebrate national holidays like the 4th of July. The intended audience is likely people who are familiar with or perpetuate racial exclusionary narratives, as the meme relies on the contrast between the visual of a joyful Black family and the hateful text to reinforce a discriminatory stereotype. The meme's hateful intent suggests it is aimed at audiences who may find the idea of Black people celebrating American patriotism offensive or inappropriate, thereby reinforcing racial hierarchies.",
